{"title":"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and into the interior of the equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are the orthogonal projections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> respectively.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/4346a46afb79842c7665c8435604e411ebfe98ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/b/51bf709ad97b61098763dc600f9b6070b2f3b6af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2BD=CE$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />, then the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/6/8d6411531f7b65667fbb52d65951037841046b21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\sqrt n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime.  Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/4/b44a897cca92fdb6fd83b8f77fd795aa3c479578.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; size(250); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(11pt)); real r = 31, t = -10; pair A = origin, B = dir(r-60), C = dir(r); pair X = -0.8 * dir(t), Y = 2 * dir(t); pair D = foot(B,X,Y), E = foot(C,X,Y); draw(A--B--C--A^^X--Y^^B--D^^C--E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,N); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,dir(B--D)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,dir(C--E)); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"192\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the intercept of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2afec04e3636c80fa3d89e5468045595151c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ED$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />.  By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertical_Angle_Theorem\" title=\"Vertical Angle Theorem\">Vertical Angle Theorem</a>,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/b/66b9f3af1ed7eb56faf12f897c75a3086e4d43e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CXE = \\angle DXB$\" width=\"141\" height=\"12\" />.  Also, since both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545dcb780c00b39826522ca2beb8452c49da65c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE \\parallel DB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e2d3868704c75a0de7586c9dbe81250981b55b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CEX \\sim \\triangle BDX$\" width=\"147\" height=\"13\" /> by AA Similarity.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/283b92114fdbe2bf0bd774e7af1cd469307f270d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2BD = CE$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/1080a31bc9262bc8a6ac545792e7f273caaef011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DX = \\tfrac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"69\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b2f5f5fcae865d5b4ccf1fc0aad177ff9ec731.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EX = \\tfrac23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"64\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the side length of the triangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa9ceef02fceb6ce053aee40f298a975e2d255fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX = \\tfrac{a}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"68\" height=\"21\" />.  By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fb515857e8c3222aa04c1ff5093e98f494dec05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB = \\tfrac{\\sqrt{a^2 - 1}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"98\" height=\"24\" />.  Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/947ac6c18fd498273403c6897cabd7bcbf7c6f6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = 60^\\circ$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />, so by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0ddba0b39f1ae85347f971f3ffafca5d0184808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX = \\sqrt{a^2 + \\tfrac19 a^2 - \\tfrac23 a^2 \\cdot \\tfrac12} = \\tfrac{a\\sqrt{7}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"267\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f82b126ff85ab110664d7ec2c1a16764884548f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A=(0,0), X=(14/3,0), D=(5,0), B=(5,-1.732); draw(A--D--B--A); dot(A); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,NW); dot(D); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,NE); dot(B); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,SE); dot(X); label(&quot;X&quot;,X,NW); label(&quot;$\\frac{a\\sqrt{7}}{3}$&quot;,(7/3,0),N); label(&quot;$\\frac13$&quot;,(14.5/3,0),N); label(&quot;$\\frac{\\sqrt{a^2-1}}{3}$&quot;,(5,-0.866),E); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,(2.5,-0.866), SW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"118\" />\n</p><p>By using the Pythagorean Theorem again, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbbb08a2a9d97fd6fc6d66e60ac1ae6439099d3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left( \\frac{a\\sqrt{7} + 1}{3} \\right)^2 + \\left( \\frac{\\sqrt{a^2 - 1}}{3} \\right)^2 &amp;= a^2 \\\\ (a\\sqrt{7} + 1)^2 + a^2 - 1 &amp;= 9a^2 \\\\ 7a^2 + 2a\\sqrt{7} + 1 + a^2 - 1 &amp;= 9a^2 \\\\ 2a\\sqrt{7} &amp;= a^2 \\\\ a &amp;= 2\\sqrt{7} \\end{align*}\" width=\"284\" height=\"172\" />\nThus, the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/5/d052fe95007ae23b14e129beaa87419489211c3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{28\\sqrt{3}}{4} = 7\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"92\" height=\"24\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/4/fe41e0660df4656097fe806c4c799b86ddd28546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest\" title=\"2006 iTest\">2006 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"